      "value": "@{5a4aaf7f758fa46d131cd36b|full_name}: That operation and other arithmetic, logic, and basic memory ops is what fundamental RISC is. I'm talking about optimizations within the UdonVM itself, not what the UdonVM runs. Any ops added to the vm should be highly optimizable, which is why I don't think any op should be handling structures that can't be determined when the UdonVM is compiled by the vrchat team.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
